msgid ""
"Before concluding there is one final thing I need to explain for you to "
"fully understand how these ActionShortcut objects work. There is a wrinkle "
"that is best understood by considering the following (old-style) PLUMED "
"input again:"
msgstr "動作を理解する最後の注意点を、旧入力で説明します。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:61
msgid ""
"As explained above, once the shortcuts have worked their magic PLUMED will "
"actually read in:"
msgstr "展開後は実際には次を読みます。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:72
msgid ""
"The wrinkle that you need to notice here is that the quantity that we are "
"asking PLUMED to print out `d1.lessthan` does not appear to be defined in "
"the above input. The quantity that we would like to print out is called "
"`d1_lessthan`. Obviously, given that the input above works, there is a "
"workaround for this problem and it is this that still remains to be "
"explained."
msgstr "出力する `d1.lessthan` が定義されず、実体は `d1_lessthan` という問題があります。動く理由は次です。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:76
msgid ""
"The workaround is that you can define output components for shortcuts just "
"as you would define output components in other ActionWithValue objects. For "
"our Distances action above we can thus write a registerKeywords method as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""
"ActionWithValue 同様に Shortcut に出力成分を登録できます。Distances の registerKeywords は、"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:88
msgid ""
"When `ActionWithArguments` tries to interpret a Value name such as "
"`d1.lessthan` it now does two things."
msgstr "`ActionWithArguments` は `d1.lessthan` に対し2つを確認します。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:90
msgid ""
"It checks if there is an ActionWithValue object with the label `d1` that has"
" a component called `d1.lessthan`."
msgstr "ラベル `d1` の ActionWithValue に `d1.lessthan` 成分があるか。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:91
msgid ""
"It checks if there is an ActionShortcut object with the label `d1`. If there"
" is such an ActionShortcut object, PLUMED checks if `lessthan` is amongst "
"the list of registered componets for that action. If that has indeed been "
"registered then PLUMED interprets `d1.lessthan` as `d1_lessthan` and "
"searches for an action with the label `d1_lessthan`"
msgstr ""
"ラベル `d1` の ActionShortcut があり、`lessthan` が登録されているか。あれば `d1.lessthan` を "
"`d1_lessthan` と解釈し、`d1_lessthan` の Action を探す。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:93
msgid ""
"Notice that this behaviour is also triggered if you use wildcards like this:"
msgstr "Wildcard でも同様です。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:100
msgid ""
"PRINT here would ouptut `d1_lessthan` and `d1_lowest` as these are the two "
"actions that are registerd and created by the DISTANCES shortcut command."
msgstr "PRINT は登録・生成された `d1_lessthan` と `d1_lowest` を出します。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:102
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "結論"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:104
msgid ""
"The new syntax for MultiColvar is (I think) clearer than the old one. It "
"also more flexible and allows one to do many more things with PLUMED. I thus"
" want to encourage users to learn it and to discard the old-style inputs in "
"future. To help with this aim, I have ensured that you have the option to "
"see the full input whenever a shortcut action appears in an example input on"
" the tutorials page and in the nest. You can try this functionality above. "
"If you hover over any of the DISTANCES commands in the example inputs above "
"you will see an option to expand the shortcut. If you click this option the "
"full three-line input for `DISTANCES LESS_THAN` is shown."
msgstr ""
"新構文はより明確・柔軟なので、今後は旧構文を置き換えることを勧めます。Tutorial・NEST では Shortcut を展開できます。上の "
"DISTANCES に Hover して展開を押すと、`DISTANCES LESS_THAN` の3行全体が見えます。"

#: MultiColvarShortcut.md:109
msgid ""
"I think that allowing users to see how code has been implemented in this way"
" is enormously useful. Users can start understanding how the code works by "
"interacting with the rich set of (automatically-annotated) examples in the "
"nest and tutorials that are likely related to the calculations they wish to "
"perform. They thus no longer need to battle through material in a manual "
"that is full of information that is not relevant to the work they are doing."
msgstr "関連する自動注釈付きの豊富な例を操作して実装を理解でき、無関係な情報も多いマニュアルと格闘せずに済みます。"
